---
description: Recover the user's actual workspace decision from its owned original conversation, saved revisions and any requested working draft.
args:
  goal: string
returns: MemoryResult
---
Establish the owned subject and source coordinates with evidence.identifyMemoryScope. Interpret which original sources the user permits and which facts or uncertainties they need. Use investigateRetainedMemory with the actual goal, brief and scoped reader capabilities to gather relevant evidence. Its readers are evidence.recallMemoryLeads, evidence.readMemoryMessages, evidence.readMemoryArchive and evidence.readMemoryDraft; keep the artifact writer outside that investigation. Search hits are leads, not original evidence.

Judge the requested claim against the actual originals with judgeMemoryClaim. Distinguish agreement, proposals, quotations, revisions, uncertainty and unsaved work using the evidence's native source identities. Give the requested explanation and authentic citations, including exact wording when requested. Preserve an honest absence of evidence rather than inventing an approval or source.

Use shouldRetainMemoryFinding to interpret a requested or conditional private record. Stage the actual brief, investigation plan, evidence and finding through evidence.stageMemoryHandoff only when the user requested that artifact and its native scope admits it. A grant does not request a note. Preserve the actual optional receipt and return applicationResult. Never revise source records, acknowledge a message, contact anyone or treat a private note as a new authorization.
